It blows our mind and I agree with you.
这让我们很震撼，我同意你的看法。

00:08:08.189 --> 00:08:26.189
I think they're very much of a similar graduating class, both in like the fact that they have lived on and gotten to kind of have new generations fall in love with them, but also that they were kind of both in their own way doing super different things in comedy at that time, things that other shows weren't doing.
我认为它们确实属于同一届“毕业班”，不仅因为它们长盛不衰，让一代又一代的新人爱上它们，还因为它们在当时都以各自独特的方式在喜剧领域做着非常不同的事情，是其他节目没有做过的事情。

00:08:26.189 --> 00:08:33.509
Yeah, they kind of both invented their own comedic vocabulary, like, in totally different ways.
是的，它们都以完全不同的方式发明了自己的喜剧词汇。

00:08:33.509 --> 00:08:36.710
But emotional, they were emos at comps.
但它们充满了情感，是情感化的情景喜剧。

00:08:36.710 --> 00:08:37.750
And that's why we liked Scrub.
这就是我们喜欢《实习医生风云》的原因。

00:08:37.750 --> 00:08:40.230
That's why we wrote a Scrubs before we ever created How Much Mother.
这就是我们在创作《老爸老妈的浪漫史》之前先看《实习医生风云》的原因。

00:08:40.230 --> 00:08:44.429
We wanted to write a show without feeling, because it could make you cry, Scrubs.
我们想写一部充满真情实感的剧，因为《实习医生风云》能让你哭泣。

00:08:44.429 --> 00:08:46.070
Congrats on it being back around.
祝贺它重新回归。

00:08:46.070 --> 00:08:50.429
Like, I want to ask you what it's like to read, we're revisiting our memories of him on a podcast.
我想问你，在播客中重温我们对他的记忆，是一种什么样的体验。

00:08:50.429 --> 00:08:52.350
You're actually like, you're going back there.
你其实就像是，你正在回到那个地方。

00:08:52.350 --> 00:08:56.950
You're actually back in the 2026 version of Scrubs, which is fascinating.
你实际上回到了2026年版本的《实习医生风云》，这太迷人了。

00:08:56.950 --> 00:08:58.309
And I want to know more about that.
我想了解更多这方面的信息。

00:08:58.309 --> 00:09:00.029
but we should talk about this episode.
但我们应该聊聊这一集。

00:09:00.029 --> 00:09:02.470
Yeah, let's talk about 10 sessions.
好的，我们来聊聊《十次约会》。

00:09:02.470 --> 00:09:05.629
Was this, I believe this was written by Carter Basin Craig Thomas, is that right?
这一集，我记得是由卡特·贝恩斯（Carter Bays）和克雷格·托马斯（Craig Thomas）写的，对吗？

00:09:05.629 --> 00:09:10.990
Yeah, this was in the melee and madness of the writer's guild strike ended.
对，这是在编剧工会罢工结束后的混乱中完成的。

00:09:10.990 --> 00:09:15.789
And then it was like, hey guys, you gotta make nine episodes in 10 and a half weeks.
当时的情况是：“嘿，伙计们，你们必须在十周半内拍出九集。”

00:09:15.789 --> 00:09:18.230
So we wrote this in a hurry.
所以我们是匆忙写出这一集的。

00:09:18.230 --> 00:09:20.470
And all of a sudden two things needed to happen.
突然之间，有两件事必须解决。

00:09:20.470 --> 00:09:24.470
We needed to figure out how we were gonna write a part for Britney Spears who had reached out.
我们需要想出如何为主动联系我们的布兰妮·斯皮尔斯（Britney Spears）写一个角色。

00:09:24.470 --> 00:09:26.870
Her people wanted her to do our show.
她的团队希望她能出演我们的节目。

00:09:26.870 --> 00:09:31.789
And two, we needed to cast this hugely important role of Stella in a hurry.
第二，我们需要仓促敲定斯特拉这个极其重要的角色。

00:09:31.789 --> 00:09:34.350
But we were all on strike and there was no way to get ahead of it.
但我们当时都在罢工，根本无法提前做准备。

00:09:34.350 --> 00:09:39.750
So we called you super last minute as I recall because we were just scrambling out of the strike.
如果我没记错的话，我们当时是以超级临时的方式给你打电话的，因为我们刚结束罢工，正手忙脚乱呢。

00:09:39.750 --> 00:09:40.750
It's astonishing.
这太惊人了。

00:09:40.750 --> 00:09:41.830
It all came together.
这一切居然都凑齐了。

00:09:41.830 --> 00:09:48.549
What is your memory of like, and did it feel weird to be getting an offer to come do like an arc on another show while you were on a show?
你对当时的记忆是什么样的？当你在拍一部剧的时候，接到邀请去另一部剧客串几集，你会觉得奇怪吗？

00:09:48.549 --> 00:09:54.789
Like, what's your memory of us asking you in this completely last minute insane way to do this?
话说，你对我们用这种完全临时、疯狂的方式邀请你有什么印象？

00:09:54.789 --> 00:09:55.789
Okay.
好吧。

00:09:55.789 --> 00:09:56.576
I loved the show.
我很喜欢这部剧。

00:09:56.576 --> 00:09:57.178
I watched it.
我看过它。

00:09:57.178 --> 00:09:57.687
I loved it.
我很喜欢。

00:09:57.687 --> 00:10:00.509
And I was actually sitting at Pinkberry with Nicole Sullivan.
当时我正和妮可·沙利文（Nicole Sullivan）坐在粉莓（Pinkberry）店里。

00:10:01.070 --> 00:10:02.815
And we were having first yogurt.
我们在吃第一轮酸奶。

00:10:02.815 --> 00:10:04.451
And I remember getting a call.
我记得我接到了一个电话。

00:10:04.451 --> 00:10:07.560
And my memory of it is that it wasn't an arc at the time.
我对这件事的记忆是，当时那并不是一个故事线（好几集），

00:10:07.560 --> 00:10:08.488
It was that week.
而是就那一周的事。

00:10:08.488 --> 00:10:09.960
It was the call that I got.
我接到的那个电话。

00:10:09.960 --> 00:10:12.197
It was come to this episode, 10 sessions.
那是来拍这一集，即第十场。

00:10:12.197 --> 00:10:13.342
And it was a Tuesday.
那是星期二。

00:10:13.342 --> 00:10:16.669
And obviously you guys have like a Monday to Friday schedule.
显然你们的工作日程是周一到周五。

00:10:16.669 --> 00:10:17.932
It was already the Tuesday.
当时已经周二了。

00:10:17.932 --> 00:10:21.998
So my recollection was that someone else is doing the part, had fallen out of the part.
所以我的记忆是，原本演这个角色的别人不演了，演不成了。

00:10:21.998 --> 00:10:23.307
I got a call on the Tuesday.
我在周二接到了电话。

00:10:23.307 --> 00:10:24.990
It was like, can you come right now?
对方说，你现在能来吗？

00:10:24.990 --> 00:10:26.668
like just drive over here.
就像是，直接开车过来就行。

00:10:26.668 --> 00:10:28.475
And I was like, yeah, great.
然后我说，好的，太棒了。

00:10:28.475 --> 00:10:28.975
I'm in.
我加入。

00:10:28.975 --> 00:10:30.265
So I drove over you.
于是我就开车去找你们了。

00:10:30.265 --> 00:10:33.234
I completely forget what that was, by the way.
顺便说一句，我完全忘了那是怎么回事了。

00:10:33.234 --> 00:10:41.237
I'm going to have to text side text Pam Friman to remind me because I'm having an old man moment because that's astonishing.
我得发短信问问帕姆·弗里曼（Pam Friman）提醒我一下，因为我有点老糊涂了，这太不可思议了。

00:10:41.237 --> 00:10:42.334
Okay, keep going.
好吧，你继续。

00:10:42.334 --> 00:10:42.834
Yeah.
好。

00:10:42.834 --> 00:10:44.254
I remember who it was.
我记得那是谁。

00:10:44.254 --> 00:10:46.448
And so we shouldn't talk about it.
所以我们不应该讨论这个。

00:10:46.448 --> 00:10:50.514
And I wrote you this little ditty to send you in New York City.
我为你写了这首小曲，打算发到纽约市给你。

00:10:50.514 --> 00:10:51.805
We'll be right back.
我们马上回来。

00:10:51.580 --> 00:10:58.720
Hi, I'm Alex Goldman, host of the Hyper-Fixed Podcast.
嗨，我是亚历克斯·戈德曼（Alex Goldman），“超级固定”播客的主持人。

00:10:58.720 --> 00:11:02.419
Each week, we take listeners' problems and try to solve them for them.
每周，我们都会接听听众的问题并试图帮他们解决。

00:11:02.419 --> 00:11:05.399
Problems like, I'm 30 and I'm scared to drive in New York.
比如这样的问题：我都30岁了，还不敢在纽约开车。

00:11:05.399 --> 00:11:09.080
Or why can't I adjust the volume of my car stereo when I'm in reverse?
或者为什么我在倒车时不能调节汽车音响的音量？

00:11:09.080 --> 00:11:11.620
We also solve non-car-related problems.
我们也解决与汽车无关的问题。

00:11:11.620 --> 00:11:17.789
If you have a problem, not only will we fix it, we'll expose the hidden systems that cause that problem in the first place.
如果你遇到了问题，我们不仅会解决它，还会揭示导致该问题的隐藏系统。

00:11:17.789 --> 00:11:20.269
That's the Hyper-Fixed Podcast from Radiotopia.
这就是来自 Radiotopia 的“超级固定”播客。

00:11:20.269 --> 00:11:39.059
at wherever you find podcasts or at hyperfixedpod.com.
你可以在任何地方收听播客，或访问 hyperfixedpod.com。

00:11:39.059 --> 00:11:45.299
So then I drove over to you guys and you guys gave me the script and we were, you guys were already in rehearsal for it.
然后我就开车去了你们那里，你们给了我剧本，而你们当时已经开始排练了。

00:11:45.299 --> 00:11:49.460
So we rehearsed and it was immediately fun.
于是我们进行了排练，而且立刻就觉得很有趣。

00:11:49.460 --> 00:12:03.899
Like it was one of those things where, you know, I loved like as an actor, the model that you guys used of like rehearsing and then the network run through and then shooting on the other few days of the week.
作为一名演员，我非常喜欢你们采用的那种模式，比如先排练，然后是电视网审片彩排（network run through），接着在一周的剩余几天里进行拍摄。

00:12:03.899 --> 00:12:13.460
what I feel like is you had the best of both worlds of it, you got the feeling of doing, you know, in front of an audience just because you had the network run through and it felt like you're doing a mini play.
我觉得你们拥有了两者最好的部分，你们既有在观众面前表演的感觉，仅仅因为你们有电视网审片彩排，感觉就像是在演一出小型话剧。

00:12:13.460 --> 00:12:14.620
A little play.
一出小话剧。

00:12:14.620 --> 00:12:15.460
A little play.
一出小话剧。

00:12:15.460 --> 00:12:20.220
And that was just like, was something super unique that like most shows don't get to do.
这非常独特，是大多数剧集都无法做到的。

00:12:20.220 --> 00:12:29.059
And then also had the benefit of the way you shot it so that you could have more flexibility in terms of getting like cool things like the two minute date.
同时它还具有你们拍摄方式带来的优势，这样你们在获取像两分钟约会这样酷炫的镜头时能有更大的灵活性。

00:12:29.059 --> 00:12:31.980
And so yeah, so I get the call, is it Pinkberry?
所以，对啊，我接到电话，是 Pinkberry 吗？

00:12:31.980 --> 00:12:33.100
Do you remember you guys?
你们还记得吗？

00:12:33.100 --> 00:12:36.100
And then that was the week before we went back to shooting scrubs.
然后那是我们回去拍《实习医生风云》前的一周。

00:12:36.539 --> 00:12:40.740
So that week I was not doing double duty, but then they called and said, we never would have gotten you if that wasn't true.
所以那一周我并没有两头跑，但后来他们打电话来说，如果不是这样，我们根本请不到你。

00:12:40.740 --> 00:12:42.820
That's the only reason we got you is that they didn't grab.
我们能请到你唯一的原因就是他们没抢先。

00:12:43.059 --> 00:12:44.899
There was a minute before they started to back up.
在他们开始倒退之前有一小会儿时间。

00:12:45.299 --> 00:12:45.899
So crazy.
太疯狂了。

00:12:45.899 --> 00:12:46.740
It's been a fun time to back up.
倒退回去也是一段有趣的时光。

00:12:46.740 --> 00:12:50.139
And then, and then after we did that episode, you guys had said, can you come back and do more?
然后，然后我们拍完那一集之后，你们就说，能不能回来拍更多？

00:12:50.139 --> 00:12:51.659
And I said, I would love to.
我说，我很乐意。

00:12:51.659 --> 00:12:54.340
And then we asked Bill Lawrence and he said, yeah, let's make it work.
然后我们问了比尔·劳伦斯，他说，行吧，我们想办法搞定。

00:12:54.620 --> 00:13:01.860
And so I remember I would wake up and come to you guys first and get into her makeup at like five and start shooting at like seven.
所以我记得我会醒来先去找你们，大概五点开始化她的妆，七点左右开始拍摄。

00:13:01.860 --> 00:13:04.580
and then I shoot to like 11.30 and then I drive to scrubs.
然后我拍到大概 11:30，接着开车去《实习医生风云》。

00:13:04.580 --> 00:13:07.259
Same lab coat, you're right, it was the same one.
同一件白大褂，你说得对，就是同一件。

00:13:07.259 --> 00:13:08.659
Easily transferable.
很容易无缝衔接。

00:13:08.659 --> 00:13:12.940
And then shoot, and so I just remember like, I didn't sleep a ton, but I loved it.
然后开拍，所以我只记得——我没怎么睡觉，但我很喜欢。

00:13:12.940 --> 00:13:13.779
It was really fun.
真的很有趣。

00:13:13.779 --> 00:13:17.620
It reminds me there's a famous story about crazy and Cynthia Nixon when she was a teenager.
这让我想起了一个关于疯狂和辛西娅·尼克松在我还是个十几岁孩子时的著名故事。

00:13:17.620 --> 00:13:19.419
She was in two Broadway shows at once.
她当时同时在演两部百老汇话剧。

00:13:19.419 --> 00:13:20.259
Do you guys know this?
你们知道这事吗？

00:13:20.259 --> 00:13:21.100
No.
不知道。

00:13:21.100 --> 00:13:29.899
She was in Hurley Burley and Tom Stoppard's The Real Thing, but she was in the first act of one of them and the second act of the other one.
她演了《浮华世界》和汤姆·斯托帕德的《真实的东西》，但她是演其中一部的第一幕，另一部的第二幕。

00:13:29.899 --> 00:13:35.700
so she would run like two blocks through an alley and join this other cast.
所以她会穿过一条小巷跑两个街区，然后加入另一个剧组。

00:13:35.700 --> 00:13:37.899
And she only, I think, took one curtain call.
而且我想她只谢幕了一次。

00:13:38.860 --> 00:13:40.779
But they made a rule that you can't do that anymore.
但他们后来定了一条规矩，说你不能再这么干了。

00:13:40.779 --> 00:13:43.179
I actually talked to her at this play because I asked her about it.
我其实在这部剧的时候跟她聊过，因为我向她问起这事。

00:13:43.179 --> 00:13:45.779
So they made a rule in Actors Act, but you can't do that anymore.
所以他们在演员公会里立了一条规矩，你不能再那样做了。

00:13:45.779 --> 00:13:47.779
And it's like the Cynthia Nixon clause.
这就叫“辛西娅·尼克松条款”。

00:13:47.779 --> 00:13:49.539
It's the Nixon clause, you're not allowed.
这就是尼克松条款，不允许这么干。

00:13:49.539 --> 00:13:50.700
But that's what you were doing.
但你当时就是在做这种事。

00:13:50.700 --> 00:13:53.779
You were the Cynthia Nixon of the Primetime sitcoms.
你就是黄金时段情景喜剧界的辛西娅·尼克松。

00:13:53.779 --> 00:13:54.779
Yeah, yeah.
对，对。

00:13:54.779 --> 00:14:02.299
I do remember reversing into a pillar in the parking garage, a parquet as we call it, Canada, and thinking like, a parquet, there it is.
我确实记得在停车场里倒车撞到了一根柱子，我们在加拿大把这叫停车场（parquet），当时还想着——一个停车场，这不就撞上了嘛。

00:14:02.299 --> 00:14:03.960
Slow down, it'll be fine when you get there.
放慢点，等你到了就没事了。

00:14:03.960 --> 00:14:04.635
Ooh.
噢。

00:14:04.635 --> 00:14:05.480
Yeah.
对。

00:14:05.480 --> 00:14:08.899
Bill Lawrence was very nice to let, to say yes to this, by the way.
顺便说一句，比尔·劳伦斯人真好，居然同意了这件事。

00:14:08.899 --> 00:14:10.019
I want to give him a big shout out.
我要好好感谢他一下。

00:14:10.019 --> 00:14:13.019
He could have easily said like, no, she's one of the stars of my show.
他完全可以说：不，她是我剧里的主演之一。

00:14:13.019 --> 00:14:14.299
You can't have her.
你们不能带走她。

00:14:14.299 --> 00:14:20.059
And I think we knew in the back of our head that we wanted more of you and that we were going to ask you back, but we didn't want to frighten anyone.
我想我们心里其实都清楚，我们还想要你演更多，也打算邀请你回来，但我们不想吓到任何人。

00:14:20.059 --> 00:14:23.179
So we said it's a one off, but really we knew it was more.
所以我们说这是一次性的客串，但实际上我们知道不仅如此。

00:14:23.179 --> 00:14:25.659
I completely forget who it was going to be first.
我完全忘了原本最开始定的是谁。

00:14:25.659 --> 00:14:31.059
I get my recollection is we were told, put this other person on as a love interest.
我的记忆是，有人告诉我们，让另一个人来演这个恋爱对象。

00:14:31.059 --> 00:14:34.019
I mean, you can't say it, right?
我是说，你不能说出来，对吧？

00:14:34.019 --> 00:14:35.500
You can't say what your memory is of it.
你不能说出你记忆中的那个人是谁。

00:14:35.500 --> 00:14:36.659
It would be too awkward.
那就太尴尬了。

00:14:36.659 --> 00:14:37.500
Question mark.
打个问号。

00:14:37.500 --> 00:14:38.419
I can after we cut.
等我们剪辑完我可以。

00:14:38.419 --> 00:14:39.259
I'll tell you guys.
我会告诉你们的。

00:14:39.259 --> 00:14:40.100
I remember.
我记得。

00:14:40.100 --> 00:14:41.980
We'll have to do it later, because I'm really forgetting it.
我们等会儿再说吧，因为我真的快忘光了。

00:14:41.980 --> 00:14:45.500
Wait, was the person fired or what happened?
等等，那个人是被解雇了还是怎么回事？

00:14:45.500 --> 00:14:49.980
Not, that wasn't information that I was pretty to, but I don't think so.
不是，这不是我能了解的信息，但我觉得应该不是。

00:14:49.980 --> 00:14:51.940
I am shocked that I can't remember this.
我很震惊我居然记不得这事了。

00:14:51.940 --> 00:14:55.460
But it's a portrait of how crazy that time was that I can't remember what this was.
但这恰恰说明了那个时期有多疯狂，以至于我都记不清这到底是怎么回事了。

00:14:55.460 --> 00:14:57.419
I'm sure it was like, all right, we'll get to it.
我敢肯定当时就是：好吧，我们以后再说。

00:14:57.419 --> 00:14:58.820
We'll go off my camera.
我们把镜头转开吧。

00:14:58.820 --> 00:15:00.340
Do you know what's so great though, Sarah?
萨拉，你知道最棒的是什么吗？

00:15:00.340 --> 00:15:05.340
Like, I love when I can be the solution to a problem.
比如，我喜欢自己能成为问题解决者的时候。

00:15:05.379 --> 00:15:09.860
Like, when they get, like can't cast something and then I step in and can do it.
就像他们找不到演员的时候，然后我挺身而出搞定它。

00:15:09.860 --> 00:15:15.299
Like, there's something actually great about that position because you're like, you're kind of just competing against yourself.
那种立场其实有种很棒的感觉，因为你会觉得，你其实只是在和自己竞争。

00:15:15.299 --> 00:15:17.620
You're like, you're actually become the hero.
你会觉得自己简直成了英雄。

