我说，这是你的第一次拍照吗？

00:28:22.819 --> 00:28:26.859
And she looked at me like, what?
她看着我，一脸震惊：什么？

00:28:26.859 --> 00:28:28.140
You nervous?
你紧张吗？

00:28:28.140 --> 00:28:37.539
I was like, you know, but I always, I always thought it was a very, I know it was like, for her, she didn't want to be spot lit in that way.
我说，你知道的，但我一直、我一直觉得这非常……我知道，对于她来说，她不想以那种方式成为聚光灯的焦点。

00:28:37.539 --> 00:28:38.619
She was like, I'm doing this show.
她当时的反应是，我在演这部剧。

00:28:38.619 --> 00:28:40.380
I'd rather like be a part of the show.
我宁愿成为这部剧的一部分。

00:28:40.380 --> 00:28:41.380
Yeah.
是啊。

00:28:41.380 --> 00:28:42.380
Yes.
没错。

00:28:42.380 --> 00:28:46.220
But she really, I was told they were like, she didn't want to do the shoot without you.
但她真的，别人告诉我，如果没有你，她不想拍这组照片。

00:28:46.220 --> 00:28:48.259
She asked if you would, would be with her.
她问你愿不愿意陪她。

00:28:48.259 --> 00:28:49.259
That's really nice.
这真的很好。

00:28:49.259 --> 00:28:53.980
And it's her, yeah, it's her wanting to say, I know I'm part, I'm joining the show for this thing.
这其实是她想表达，我知道我是其中的一部分，我为了这件事加入了这部剧。

00:28:53.980 --> 00:28:57.180
It's not the me show and that was her, that was her energy.
这不是以我为主角的个人秀，这就是她的状态，她的态度。

00:28:57.180 --> 00:29:00.740
She knew how to fit into the episode and do what was needed.
她知道如何融入这一集并做好需要做的事。

00:29:00.740 --> 00:29:23.099
There was something, I was really startled at her innocence, her ability to play, not play, I'm not playing three different meanings to this, I'm playing the surface level which is where that character lived, but it was so sincere and so sweet and it was even funnier than I remembered it and I remembered it being funny.
有一点，她的天真让我大为震惊，她那种表演的能力——不是在演，我没有赋予它三种不同的含义，我只是在展现表面那一层，那个角色所处的世界——但它是如此真诚、如此甜美，而且比我记忆中还要好笑，而我本来就记得它挺搞笑的。

00:29:23.099 --> 00:29:24.500
I totally agree.
我完全赞同。

00:29:24.500 --> 00:29:36.140
And when she went and did that piece with Neil, where Abby and Barney come in the turquoise like v-neck sweaters, and she's pretending they're doing the bit together, or he's doing the bit to bug.
当她和尼尔一起演那场戏时，艾比和巴尼穿着蓝绿色的V领毛衣进来了，她假装他们在一起拍段子，或者说他为了烦人而拍那个段子。

00:29:36.140 --> 00:29:37.140
Yes.
是的。

00:29:37.140 --> 00:29:38.140
And I'm glad that's your character.
我很庆幸那是你的角色。

00:29:38.140 --> 00:29:40.140
Like a couple episodes later.
就像几集之后的事。

00:29:40.140 --> 00:29:41.140
Yeah.
对。

00:29:41.140 --> 00:29:42.140
And she was fantastic.
她表现得棒极了。

00:29:42.140 --> 00:29:46.660
And in that same way, you know, like just kind of buying the fact that he's proposing to her.
同样地，你知道的，就好像完全相信他在向她求婚一样。

00:29:46.660 --> 00:29:47.660
She's good.
她很不错。

00:29:47.660 --> 00:29:48.660
She's a good guy.
她是个好人。

00:29:48.660 --> 00:29:49.660
She's like she really...
她真的……

00:29:49.660 --> 00:29:51.940
It must have gone well for her that she came back.
她后来又回来了，这对她来说一定很顺利吧。

00:29:51.940 --> 00:29:52.940
You know what I mean?
你知道我的意思吗？

00:29:52.940 --> 00:30:22.319
I remember Pam being incredibly kind to her, like just achingly kind because I think there was a sense of like, this poor girl, it was like, almost what we were, I gave Craig this award the other night, Sarah, at this event and Monica Lewinsky, who's a friend of mine, but she was honored and she talked a lot about how when other people tell your story and it takes your story away from you and you're not allowed to tell your own story.
我记得帕姆对她好得难以置信，那种让人心疼的好，因为我觉得大家有一种感觉，这个可怜的女孩……萨拉，前几天我在一个活动上把这个奖颁给了克雷格，而我的朋友莫妮卡·莱温斯基也受到了表彰，她谈了很多关于当别人讲述你的故事时，会剥夺你讲述自己故事的权力，让你无法讲述自己的故事。

00:30:22.319 --> 00:30:45.589
And as, you know, her podcast called Reclaiming, and I felt like that was kind of Britney Spears like first step on the road back to reclaiming her own story, because it had been absolutely hijacked from her and this old man, he musted me, fell in love with you, New York City.
正如你所知，她的播客叫《夺回》，我觉得这就像是布兰妮·斯皮尔斯夺回自己故事的第一步，因为她的故事绝对被劫持了，而这个老头，他让我着迷，爱上了你，纽约市。

00:30:45.589 --> 00:30:59.142
And now commercials, end of commercials back to show, you, you, you, you, you, you started having a lot of scrutiny on you at a young age Sarah, right?
现在是广告时间，广告结束回到节目，萨拉，你很小的时候就开始受到很多关注了，对吧？

00:30:59.142 --> 00:31:05.425
You were like, you've begun this job pretty, this career pretty early.
你很早就开始从事这份工作、这项事业了。

00:31:05.425 --> 00:31:09.194
You must have had some connection to that.
你一定对此深有感触。

00:31:09.194 --> 00:31:21.850
It seems when you're talking about your memories of Britain, you seem like you have a great deal of empathy for where she was at this moment.
当你在谈论对布兰妮的记忆时，你似乎对她当时的处境有着极大的共情。

00:31:21.849 --> 00:31:28.233
Yeah, I mean, I would never even begin to compare, like I had, you know, I had started doing musical theater as a kid.
是的，我是说，我绝不会把这拿来比较，我小时候就开始演音乐剧了。

00:31:28.233 --> 00:31:33.210
I was actually like professionally working until grade 12, which is Canadian for 12th grade.
我其实从12年级开始就进行专业工作了，“12年级”是加拿大的说法。

00:31:33.210 --> 00:31:51.809
And I feel like at that point, yeah, it was sort of like jumping into all of it at once, because it was like the number one show, Roseanne was number one show on TV at the time, and I had really barely worked and kind of had no business being there.
我觉得在那个时候，是的，就好像一下子陷入了这一切，因为这是收视率第一的节目，《罗斯anne》当时是电视上收视第一的节目，而我其实几乎没有演过什么，根本不应该出现在那里。

00:31:51.809 --> 00:32:06.930
And I do remember that feeling of all of it happening at once, both getting recognized and being at an age where you kind of just want to blend, you're like about to go into first university and that was when it was carrying through and to that time and just kind of like all of it.
我确实记得那种一切同时发生的感觉，既被认出来，又处于这样一个年龄：你只想融入人群，你即将上大学，而这种状态一直持续着，直到那个时候，所有的这一切扑面而来。

00:32:06.930 --> 00:32:15.049
Like I remember going to the first red carpet and I had a pair of shoes and my mom was like do you want to buy shoes that actually match the dress you're wearing and I'm like why would I do that?
就像我记得去参加第一次红毯时，我有一双鞋，我妈问我：你想买双真正配得上你身上这条裙子的鞋吗？我说：我为什么要那样做？

00:32:15.049 --> 00:32:20.049
I have a perfectly good pair of shoes and I went up on the worst dress list and I didn't really care about that but it was like so real.
我有一双完全可以穿的鞋啊。结果我上了最差着装榜，我其实并不在意那个，但这一切是如此真实。

00:32:20.049 --> 00:32:21.769
It was like that kind of thing, right?
就像那种感觉，对吧？

00:32:21.769 --> 00:32:30.890
Like you're sort of going like okay I'm you know show up on Sunday it's Battle of the Network and I'm like, okay, and I get there, and I'm like, where's the rest of my cast?
就像你有点那种感觉，好吧，你知道的，周日去参加“网络明星对抗赛”，而我心想，好吧，我到了那里，然后心想，我的其他演员队友呢？

00:32:30.890 --> 00:32:44.130
I just thought it was like something you did, but it was superstar American gladiators, and they hand you like sports bra and hot pants, and there's like a volcano with a gladiator at the top, and you're clambering up a wet volcano in spandex.
我只是以为这是某种常规通告，结果却是超级巨星美国角斗士，他们发给你一件运动内衣和热裤，现场还有一个顶部站着角斗士的火山，你就穿着紧身衣在一个湿漉漉的火山上往上爬。

00:32:44.130 --> 00:32:45.650
Wait, you said you never played sports?
等等，你刚才说你从来不运动？

00:32:45.650 --> 00:32:47.289
That sounds like sports.
听起来这挺像运动的。

00:32:47.289 --> 00:32:48.410
That and the two men's day.
那就只有这个和双人日了。

00:32:48.410 --> 00:32:49.730
That's the nerves, that's the nerves.
这就是紧张，这就是紧张。

00:32:49.730 --> 00:32:54.089
Those are my two, that's that and limbo, and race walking, that's all I got.
这就是我的两项，就这个、 limbo（林堡舞）和竞走，我就会这些。

00:32:54.089 --> 00:33:01.950
But I feel like, yeah, there were so many things like that where it was just like baptism by fire and you kind of jumping into it.
但我觉得，是的，有很多那样的事情，就像是被烈火洗礼，然后你不得不硬着头皮跳进去。

00:33:01.950 --> 00:33:16.920
And I guess, you know, I can't imagine though, like that was such a microcosm, like a 0.001% of what her life must have felt like.
我想，你知道的，我还是无法想象，那只是一个极小的缩影，大概占她生活真实感受的百分之零点零零一。

00:33:16.920 --> 00:33:20.279
Yeah, I mean, she, she seemed, she carried that with her.
对，我的意思是，她，她似乎，她一直带着那种状态。

00:33:20.279 --> 00:33:31.640
I remember like when the cameras were off, she seemed like she wanted, I understand what you say when you're like, I used up my three things because the energy was like, how do I talk to her?
我记得当摄像机关掉的时候，她看起来像是想要，我明白你说的“我用完了我的三件事”是什么意思，因为当时的能量场是：我该怎么跟她说话？

00:33:31.640 --> 00:33:33.079
How do I connect with her?
我该怎么跟她建立联系？

00:33:33.079 --> 00:33:34.920
Or does she not want that?
还是说她根本不想这样？

00:33:34.920 --> 00:33:38.920
And I think that's, her whole life is everyone around her was feeling that way.
我想这就是，她的一生中，身边的每个人都在那种感受中。

00:33:38.920 --> 00:33:40.039
And how do you connect with her?
而你又该如何与她建立联系？

00:33:40.039 --> 00:33:45.880
And it must be a very lonely feeling to know that everyone is trying to figure out how to talk to you and if they should.
知道每个人都在琢磨该怎么跟你说话、是否应该跟你说话，这一定是一种非常孤独的感觉。

00:33:45.880 --> 00:33:49.319
And that's a spooky climate to live in.
那是一种令人毛骨悚然的生活环境。

00:33:49.319 --> 00:33:50.240
Yeah.
是的。

00:33:50.240 --> 00:33:54.799
Yeah, it's, fame is, Jordana and I have talked about this.
是的，名气这东西，乔丹娜和我讨论过这个。

00:33:54.799 --> 00:34:16.400
like she thinks that sudden fame or even infamy, like when the culture just spotlights you and kind of lifts you up and tears you down, like she thinks that should be in the DSM as a like mental disorder of what it can do to you of how destabilizing it can be.
就像她认为突如其来的名气，甚至是恶名，当文化浪潮把聚光灯打在你身上，把你高高托起然后又狠狠撕碎时，她认为这应该被列入《精神疾病诊断与统计手册》（DSM），作为一种心理障碍，看看它会对你造成什么影响，看它能带来多大的颠覆性。

00:34:16.400 --> 00:34:26.719
And there, I don't think there's been enough kind of research in certain ways into how just the roller coaster of all of that.
而且我认为，对于这一切宛如过山车般的经历，在某些方面还没有进行足够多的研究。

00:34:27.840 --> 00:34:33.920
And also like, yeah, I was genuinely confused how to talk to her and approach her.
还有就是，是的，我当时真的很困惑该怎么跟她说话、怎么接近她。

00:34:33.920 --> 00:34:37.320
And like exactly what you said, like, does she want to talk to us?
就像你刚才说的，她到底想不想跟我们说话？

00:34:37.320 --> 00:34:44.639
Like, I'm sure she was like aching to be a normal person who could just shoot the shit, you know?
我觉得她肯定渴望成为一个能随便扯淡的普通人，你知道吗？

00:34:44.639 --> 00:34:49.639
But I felt like we dealt with it as well as we could.
但我觉得我们已经尽自己所能去处理好了。

00:34:49.639 --> 00:34:50.559
as well as we could.
尽我们所能去处理好了。

00:34:50.559 --> 00:34:56.320
I mean, we were trying to create a very safe space for her as we were trying to do for all the guest stars.
我的意思是，我们在努力为她创造一个非常安全的空间，就像我们为所有客串明星做的那样。

00:34:56.320 --> 00:35:03.880
But this was like our first real, like, we had a lot of like wild kind of celebrity appearances on the show.
但这可以说是我们的第一个真正的，我们在剧中有过很多那种疯狂的名人客串。

00:35:03.880 --> 00:35:05.320
You guys had amazing guest stars on that show.
你们在那个剧里有超级棒的客串明星。

00:35:05.320 --> 00:35:06.320
A cool run.
一段很酷的经历。

00:35:06.320 --> 00:35:12.679
But this one I think was, it was on another level of something culturally.
但我觉得这一次，在文化层面上达到了另一个高度。

00:35:12.679 --> 00:35:13.519
This was different.
这次不一样。

00:35:13.519 --> 00:35:14.800
Yeah, this was different.
是的，这次不一样。

