My memory of my weird experience with her was We were having some sort of a relaunch party.
我对跟她那次奇特经历的记忆是，我们当时正在办某种重新开播的派对。

00:35:20.320 --> 00:35:23.320
There was a publicity party for High Match Mother that week, Sarah.
莎拉，那周有一场为《老爸老妈浪漫史》举办的宣传派对。

00:35:23.320 --> 00:35:34.519
I mean, you probably couldn't come because you probably were shooting scrubs later that night or going to, you don't remember, I have no memory of the party, really, but it was like a publicity, like we're back on the air.
我的意思是，你可能没能来，因为你那天晚上晚些时候可能在拍《实习医生风云》或者要去……你记不清了，我对那个派对其实没什么记忆，但它就像是一个宣传活动，宣告我们重返荧屏。

00:35:34.519 --> 00:35:38.239
It was an event, it was all schmoozy and very Hollywood.
这是一个活动，充满了交际应酬，非常的好莱坞。

00:35:38.239 --> 00:36:40.800
And I was, somehow I got voted to invite Britney Spears to it and I was given a card, like a little card, invitation card and like center her trailer that was for her and like I knocked on her door and she opened the door and I kind of got this like these sweats where she's like I'm about to ask how Britney Spears on a date basically like I've got this little invitation like hey Britney this is probably stupid we've got this thing on Thursday night me I don't know if it's probably dumb but maybe when I come and like awkwardly asked her out to this thing essentially and like and she was like very pledge is like thank you and I remember like walking away and being like why did I agree to do this who like I don't know how I got voted to be the person to do this but I basically like failed at asking out Britney Spears because she did not come to the event but it is it was one of those events that you I felt this you know when the when the Victoria's secret models were on it's just one of those events where Sarah you know everyone's in a while you because I think when you when you're on a TV show you metabolize it pretty quickly You're like, this is my job.
不知怎么的，我被推选去邀请布兰妮·斯皮尔斯参加，他们给了我一张卡片，一张小卡片，邀请卡，让我送到她的化妆车里，那是给她的。我去敲了她的门，她开门的那一刻，我开始冒虚汗，心想我就快要问布兰妮·斯皮尔斯约会了，基本上就是我拿着这张小卡片——“嘿，布兰妮，这可能挺蠢的，我们周四晚上有个活动，我不知道这大概很傻，但也许你可以来……”——就这样笨拙地开口邀请她去参加这个活动。而她非常客气地说：“谢谢。”我记得我走开的时候心想：我怎么会同意做这种事？我不知道我是怎么被推选出来做这件事的人，但我基本上是把邀请布兰妮·斯皮尔斯约会这件事搞砸了，因为她没有来参加活动。但这确实是那种你会……我能感受到这一点，你知道的，当维多利亚的秘密模特来客串时，这就像是那种活动，莎拉，你懂的，偶尔会有这种时刻——因为我觉得当你拍电视剧时，你很快就能消化这种状态。你会觉得，这就是我的工作。

00:36:40.800 --> 00:36:42.639
These are my coworkers, no big deal.
这些是我的同事，没什么大不了的。

00:36:42.639 --> 00:36:47.920
But then there's every once in a while, something comes along that you're like, life is weird out here.
但偶尔会有那么一刻，有些事情出现，让你觉得：外面的生活真奇妙啊。

00:36:47.920 --> 00:36:55.960
Like this is a strange, I'm the only person from my high school class that is currently like having this weirdness in their life, you know?
就像这是一种奇怪的体验，我是我高中同学里唯一一个目前生活中正在经历这种怪异事情的人，你知道吗？

00:36:55.960 --> 00:36:57.760
A hundred percent.
百分之百。

